00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:04,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:07,345
I want Mariko to be happy.

2
00:00:08,413 --> 00:00:09,380
But…

3
00:00:09,447 --> 00:00:14,986
You have been continually committing
criminal acts all this time.

4
00:00:15,487 --> 00:00:17,856
I was wrong the whole time.

5
00:00:17,922 --> 00:00:21,459
Don't you decide what my happiness is!

6
00:00:21,526 --> 00:00:24,429
Me disappearing is what's best for Mariko.

7
00:00:25,296 --> 00:00:28,199
That's how I can protect
Mariko's happiness.

8
00:00:41,446 --> 00:00:43,448
‎BEST FOR MARIKO

9
00:00:43,515 --> 00:00:44,349
Doing things on your own

10
00:00:44,949 --> 00:00:47,585
without my knowledge,
claiming it was for me?

11
00:00:48,319 --> 00:00:50,855
That's just creepy! All of it is creepy!

12
00:00:51,623 --> 00:00:54,592
Doing things without Mariko's knowledge

13
00:00:55,593 --> 00:00:56,761
is bad.

14
00:01:00,398 --> 00:01:02,534
If you leave my side,
I will never forgive you!

15
00:01:03,368 --> 00:01:06,404
I will never forgive you.

16
00:01:06,971 --> 00:01:09,274
Leaving Mariko's side

17
00:01:10,575 --> 00:01:11,409
is bad.

18
00:01:14,012 --> 00:01:16,114
BAD

19
00:01:16,881 --> 00:01:21,186
What am I supposed to do
for Mariko from now on?

20
00:01:24,255 --> 00:01:25,323
MARIKO

21
00:01:25,390 --> 00:01:26,257
POST

22
00:01:28,193 --> 00:01:30,061
COMMENTS

23
00:01:32,864 --> 00:01:36,568
Up until now, I would have gathered
information on this person

24
00:01:36,634 --> 00:01:40,538
and observed whether they were a risk
factor threatening Mariko's smile, but…

25
00:01:41,673 --> 00:01:44,809
What you are doing is stalking.

26
00:01:50,014 --> 00:01:52,383
I LIKE GOING TO CAFES

27
00:01:52,450 --> 00:01:54,052
MARIKO 08

28
00:01:54,118 --> 00:01:55,687
UNFOLLOW

29
00:01:58,122 --> 00:01:59,357
UNFOLLOW

30
00:01:59,424 --> 00:02:00,992
FOLLOW

31
00:02:02,827 --> 00:02:05,463
This isn't my job anymore.

32
00:02:13,805 --> 00:02:15,273
Yukimura…

33
00:02:17,275 --> 00:02:18,443
I'm sorry.

34
00:02:18,509 --> 00:02:19,644
Yukimura!

35
00:02:20,311 --> 00:02:21,446
Sota Yukimura.

36
00:02:23,181 --> 00:02:25,350
The boy you're looking for

37
00:02:26,651 --> 00:02:27,785
is at our company.

38
00:02:27,852 --> 00:02:29,254
His name is Sota Yukimura.

39
00:02:38,263 --> 00:02:40,898
It's the darkest
under the street lamp, huh?

40
00:02:43,534 --> 00:02:46,871
So they're childhood friends
and coworkers?

41
00:02:46,938 --> 00:02:48,206
What the hell?

42
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:51,542
If that's the case, you should have
just told me from the start.

43
00:03:46,164 --> 00:03:49,233
-Let me go! Help me!
-Somebody!

44
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:51,302
Somebody, please come!

45
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:58,943
THE SERIAL KIDNAPPINGS OFF STREETS
IN SETAGAYA

46
00:04:03,247 --> 00:04:04,782
NAME: SOTA YUKIMURA

47
00:04:04,849 --> 00:04:07,352
The fact that I was present
at two murder scenes…

48
00:04:08,453 --> 00:04:09,387
I think it was also due

49
00:04:10,054 --> 00:04:14,992
to someone's intention,
someone pulling the strings.

50
00:04:38,850 --> 00:04:40,451
Wow, this is amazing.

51
00:04:40,518 --> 00:04:41,886
It doesn't use PET at all.

52
00:04:41,953 --> 00:04:44,822
That's right. It's composed of Melittin,

53
00:04:44,889 --> 00:04:46,858
which gives it its lightness.

54
00:04:46,924 --> 00:04:50,728
It's pretty boundary-pushing,
even in terms of price range.

55
00:04:51,562 --> 00:04:53,398
This will definitely sell.

56
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,301
Goodbye.

57
00:04:57,368 --> 00:04:59,103
-See you.
-Goodbye.

58
00:05:01,906 --> 00:05:03,174
Bye.

59
00:05:03,241 --> 00:05:05,143
-Goodbye.
-Bye.

60
00:05:15,887 --> 00:05:17,922
He lives alone, doesn't he?

61
00:05:18,790 --> 00:05:21,259
So why is he buying so much?

62
00:05:23,194 --> 00:05:24,195
So?

63
00:05:24,262 --> 00:05:27,098
What on earth are you doing?

64
00:05:28,466 --> 00:05:29,667
Hey, hey, hey.

65
00:05:31,235 --> 00:05:33,438
Should we keep an eye on that guy?

66
00:05:34,572 --> 00:05:35,640
Yes…

67
00:05:36,941 --> 00:05:39,210
He was investigating me
without my knowledge.

68
00:05:40,578 --> 00:05:43,247
He might be a very dangerous person.

69
00:05:43,314 --> 00:05:46,250
It looks like he even checked
my social media.

70
00:05:46,317 --> 00:05:47,852
He was creeping around?

71
00:05:48,453 --> 00:05:50,455
So what does that mean, he's a stalker?

72
00:05:51,422 --> 00:05:53,424
He's even been questioned by the police.

73
00:05:54,058 --> 00:05:55,726
We can't let our guard down.

74
00:05:55,793 --> 00:05:57,061
-I'll throw these in.
-Wow.

75
00:05:57,128 --> 00:06:01,399
I'm a manager, so I need to know
for the safety of everyone at work

76
00:06:01,466 --> 00:06:03,601
-Ah, he moved.
-Let's follow him.

77
00:06:09,774 --> 00:06:13,544
At this rate,
you look more like a stalker.

78
00:06:14,378 --> 00:06:15,513
Me?

79
00:06:16,514 --> 00:06:18,416
It can't be helped.

80
00:06:18,483 --> 00:06:21,686
You want to know everything
about the person you like, right?

81
00:06:22,887 --> 00:06:25,690
Ah, well, I have experience with that too.

82
00:06:25,756 --> 00:06:28,893
-Was it back in middle school…
-I am a manager!

83
00:06:37,201 --> 00:06:39,136
What is he looking at?

84
00:06:39,203 --> 00:06:40,204
LOOKING FOR DOG

85
00:06:40,271 --> 00:06:41,205
"He's friendly…"

86
00:06:41,272 --> 00:06:42,206
GRILLED MEAT

87
00:06:42,273 --> 00:06:43,207
MUSHROOMS

88
00:06:45,309 --> 00:06:47,712
-Oh, oh, oh!
-Oh!

89
00:06:47,778 --> 00:06:49,046
Oh, no!

90
00:06:49,647 --> 00:06:50,681
Are you okay?

91
00:06:50,748 --> 00:06:52,450
I'm sorry, I'm sorry…

92
00:06:52,517 --> 00:06:54,285
Thank you.

93
00:06:54,352 --> 00:06:55,953
-You're a lifesaver.
-Are you okay now?

94
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:57,989
-Thank you!
-No, it was no problem.

95
00:06:58,055 --> 00:06:59,524
-Over this way.
-I see.

96
00:06:59,590 --> 00:07:02,593
-How about some tea?
-Kind to the elderly.

97
00:07:02,660 --> 00:07:03,494
-Well…
-That's okay.

98
00:07:03,561 --> 00:07:04,695
High points, huh?

99
00:07:04,762 --> 00:07:06,497
That's right.

100
00:07:06,564 --> 00:07:09,100
Kind people really are the best.

101
00:07:10,568 --> 00:07:12,069
Hmm, I see…

102
00:07:20,711 --> 00:07:21,612
Let's go.

103
00:07:28,586 --> 00:07:31,455
Why has he been here so long?

104
00:07:32,256 --> 00:07:34,425
It's been quite a while.

105
00:07:34,492 --> 00:07:39,130
He's not suspicious or anything
like that, but I'm worried now.

106
00:07:40,965 --> 00:07:43,734
Now that I've stopped
investigating Mariko,

107
00:07:44,535 --> 00:07:48,506
I have insane amounts of time on my hands.

108
00:07:49,674 --> 00:07:52,944
Assuming the average
male lifespan is 80 years,

109
00:07:53,010 --> 00:07:55,246
I've got 49 more years to go.

110
00:07:55,313 --> 00:07:59,050
Working eight hours a day,
sleeping seven hours.

111
00:07:59,984 --> 00:08:02,153
Remaining nine hours of free time,

112
00:08:02,219 --> 00:08:04,889
multiplied by 49 years.

113
00:08:05,590 --> 00:08:07,758
What should I spend them doing?

114
00:08:08,459 --> 00:08:12,129
So that I don't end up looking into
Mariko, I should start a new hobby.

115
00:08:13,030 --> 00:08:14,899
Movies… I'll watch movies or something!

116
00:08:16,667 --> 00:08:17,835
Marvel…

117
00:08:18,936 --> 00:08:20,171
Mariko…

118
00:08:20,671 --> 00:08:21,639
What?

119
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:24,308
Should I start taking lessons?

120
00:08:24,375 --> 00:08:25,509
Coffee classes?

121
00:08:25,576 --> 00:08:26,677
What, what?

122
00:08:27,578 --> 00:08:30,448
Coffee… Cafe latte…

123
00:08:31,082 --> 00:08:32,350
Mariko…

124
00:08:32,416 --> 00:08:34,251
What?

125
00:08:34,318 --> 00:08:37,688
I wonder if I can donate my time
to people in this world

126
00:08:38,289 --> 00:08:41,225
who are struggling
with not having enough time.

127
00:08:45,796 --> 00:08:48,199
I'm hungry.

128
00:08:48,265 --> 00:08:50,935
I bet you are. Shall we go home?

129
00:08:53,571 --> 00:08:55,473
-Sota!
-It's Tomoya!

130
00:08:55,539 --> 00:08:57,842
-Tomoya!
-Huh?

131
00:08:57,908 --> 00:09:00,711
-Do you know her?
-What's everyone doing here?

132
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:03,948
Is this Izumi's daughter?

133
00:09:04,548 --> 00:09:06,517
Yes, this is Sara.

134
00:09:06,584 --> 00:09:08,019
Hello.

135
00:09:08,085 --> 00:09:09,320
She's Sara.

136
00:09:10,054 --> 00:09:11,322
Hello.

137
00:09:13,090 --> 00:09:16,060
So, what are you all doing
in a place like this?

138
00:09:16,127 --> 00:09:17,995
We just were around.

139
00:09:19,196 --> 00:09:20,031
A coincidence.

140
00:09:20,097 --> 00:09:22,867
We just happened to be passing by.

141
00:09:22,933 --> 00:09:24,702
-Oh, really?
-Really, we just happened to be here.

142
00:09:29,407 --> 00:09:30,541
Well then,

143
00:09:31,108 --> 00:09:33,077
-why don't we all eat together?
-Right?

144
00:09:33,144 --> 00:09:33,978
Yes, let's go!

145
00:09:34,045 --> 00:09:36,180
-Yes, let's do that!
-Yes.

146
00:09:37,148 --> 00:09:38,382
Ah, I'm sorry,

147
00:09:38,449 --> 00:09:39,750
-I'm leaving.
-Huh?

148
00:09:40,985 --> 00:09:42,920
Hey. Sota.

149
00:09:45,189 --> 00:09:47,124
Why don't we go home too?

150
00:09:47,191 --> 00:09:48,359
What?

151
00:09:51,128 --> 00:09:52,063
Hey!

152
00:09:56,567 --> 00:09:58,969
TAISUKE SAKURA

153
00:10:05,042 --> 00:10:06,010
MARIKO NOSE

154
00:10:09,714 --> 00:10:11,882
GINJIRO NOSE

155
00:10:16,721 --> 00:10:18,656
This is Sakura from the Tokyo
Metropolitan Police Department.

156
00:10:22,126 --> 00:10:23,694
That was a great idea I had.

157
00:10:23,761 --> 00:10:25,396
What did you do that for?

158
00:10:25,463 --> 00:10:27,698
-Sorry.
-That seemed like something

159
00:10:27,765 --> 00:10:30,434
Mariko would have been into too,
but then it was ruined.

160
00:10:30,501 --> 00:10:31,635
Do you want the dumplings boiled or fried?

161
00:10:33,137 --> 00:10:34,605
Uh, fried.

162
00:11:17,782 --> 00:11:18,916
What are you doing?

163
00:11:19,517 --> 00:11:21,485
No, nothing.

164
00:11:26,690 --> 00:11:27,625
Did you read them?

165
00:11:28,959 --> 00:11:31,629
Not yet. I just wondered what they were,

166
00:11:32,730 --> 00:11:33,631
so I held it for a second.

167
00:11:36,534 --> 00:11:38,102
Seriously, I swear to God.

168
00:11:46,377 --> 00:11:49,146
Come to think of it, I meant to tell you
the other day, but couldn't.

169
00:11:49,213 --> 00:11:50,948
I got a huge piece of info.

170
00:11:51,015 --> 00:11:52,383
-A huge piece of info?
-Yeah.

171
00:11:52,449 --> 00:11:54,752
Um, at that Sayuri person's funeral,

172
00:11:54,819 --> 00:11:58,255
I overheard Mariko
and her younger brother talking.

173
00:11:58,823 --> 00:12:00,491
Sayuri said to the president,

174
00:12:01,058 --> 00:12:08,032
"You haven't forgotten that you and I
share the same secret, have you?"

175
00:12:09,066 --> 00:12:10,367
The same secret?

176
00:12:11,335 --> 00:12:12,770
I just gave you crazy info, right?

177
00:12:12,837 --> 00:12:14,371
You could investigate it--

178
00:12:14,438 --> 00:12:16,540
-No, it's fine.
-Huh?

179
00:12:17,074 --> 00:12:19,810
That's not something for me to do.

180
00:12:21,312 --> 00:12:22,646
The police…

181
00:12:23,781 --> 00:12:25,449
That detective is on it.

182
00:12:27,051 --> 00:12:28,385
I shouldn't do it.

183
00:12:29,753 --> 00:12:31,188
What?

184
00:12:31,255 --> 00:12:32,156
I mean,

185
00:12:32,690 --> 00:12:37,027
two people in her circle have been killed,
and right now, Mariko might be in danger.

186
00:12:37,094 --> 00:12:38,395
I can't.

187
00:12:39,763 --> 00:12:41,999
It's not something I should do.

188
00:12:50,808 --> 00:12:53,744
I shouldn't have spoken to her that day.

189
00:12:54,745 --> 00:12:56,580
You can put hers together with mine.

190
00:12:59,750 --> 00:13:03,153
I was a person who shouldn't
have appeared before Mariko.

191
00:13:04,655 --> 00:13:08,292
No, I guess meeting 25 years ago

192
00:13:08,359 --> 00:13:11,528
and falling in love with her was wrong.

193
00:13:11,595 --> 00:13:13,797
That's not it.

194
00:13:14,398 --> 00:13:16,000
That's not where your mistake is.

195
00:13:17,935 --> 00:13:20,170
Actually, you've been wrong
the whole time.

196
00:13:20,237 --> 00:13:22,106
You've done nothing but wrong things.

197
00:13:23,507 --> 00:13:25,776
So why are you trying to act proper
all of a sudden?

198
00:13:32,983 --> 00:13:36,086
You know, I really hate that part of you.

199
00:13:36,787 --> 00:13:38,756
Why are you backing off?

200
00:13:40,391 --> 00:13:43,093
You've loved her
for 25 years, right? Twenty-five years!

201
00:13:43,761 --> 00:13:45,963
Even if you back off,
it's not like your feelings will subside.

202
00:13:46,664 --> 00:13:48,098
If you take Mariko away from your life,

203
00:13:48,165 --> 00:13:51,635
-what's left for you?
-I don't want to scare Mariko anymore!

204
00:13:52,536 --> 00:13:53,971
It was all wrong.

205
00:13:54,972 --> 00:13:56,407
All of it.

206
00:13:56,473 --> 00:14:00,878
I'm not allowed to move forward,
nor to go back.

207
00:14:01,745 --> 00:14:05,249
Then, at that company, in that department,

208
00:14:05,849 --> 00:14:08,819
just treat her normally,
like a normal person would.

209
00:14:09,853 --> 00:14:10,921
Stop sneaking around in secret

210
00:14:10,988 --> 00:14:13,657
-and just interact with her normally.
-That's impossible for me.

211
00:14:13,724 --> 00:14:15,392
Whenever Mariko
is in trouble or suffering,

212
00:14:15,459 --> 00:14:16,794
I end up wanting to do something.

213
00:14:17,361 --> 00:14:18,295
It's just like a diet.

214
00:14:18,362 --> 00:14:20,698
When you're told you can eat just a bit,
holding back is extremely painful,

215
00:14:20,764 --> 00:14:23,801
but if it's completely off-limits,
looking or getting close is off-limits,

216
00:14:23,867 --> 00:14:26,403
then I can think of it as something
that doesn't exist in this world.

217
00:14:27,504 --> 00:14:29,239
That's why it's better
not to get involved anymore.

218
00:14:29,807 --> 00:14:31,041
What the hell is that?

219
00:14:31,108 --> 00:14:33,844
What is with you? I don't give a damn.
I've never been on a diet!

220
00:14:37,047 --> 00:14:41,318
You know, I'm sick and tired of listening
to your endless rambling excuses.

221
00:14:43,988 --> 00:14:46,523
You've never faced Mariko
in a proper way to begin with.

222
00:14:47,157 --> 00:14:48,759
Why are you trying to act proper now?

223
00:14:49,827 --> 00:14:52,463
-But--
-You're the one who has protected her.

224
00:14:53,397 --> 00:14:56,967
Listen, what will you do
if she actually is in danger right now?

225
00:14:57,801 --> 00:15:00,337
Are you going to leave it to some
other guy who randomly popped up?

226
00:15:00,404 --> 00:15:02,506
You're gonna ignore it?
You're out of your mind!

227
00:15:04,808 --> 00:15:06,844
You're saying weird things too, Tomoya.

228
00:15:07,378 --> 00:15:08,812
Telling me to date her
normally one moment,

229
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:11,982
-then to not to pretend to be normal--
-I don't care

230
00:15:12,049 --> 00:15:14,785
whether you're a stalker
or whether Mariko hates you!

231
00:15:17,654 --> 00:15:20,224
Even so, protecting Mariko
is your job, isn't it?

232
00:15:25,963 --> 00:15:27,264
I'm going home.

233
00:15:59,730 --> 00:16:00,898
I'm home.

234
00:16:01,465 --> 00:16:02,933
Welcome back.

235
00:16:08,005 --> 00:16:09,573
Where's Keito?

236
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:11,742
He said he was going to a friend's place.

237
00:16:13,043 --> 00:16:14,144
I see…

238
00:16:14,211 --> 00:16:17,114
I wonder if that boy's okay.

239
00:16:18,148 --> 00:16:20,717
I guess he wouldn't be…

240
00:16:21,852 --> 00:16:23,720
Oh, Mariko, you're home?

241
00:16:24,655 --> 00:16:26,123
I have something to talk about.

242
00:16:28,258 --> 00:16:29,226
Mariko.

243
00:16:29,293 --> 00:16:32,796
Sakura, why are you at our home?

244
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:38,368
-Thank you.
-Sure.

245
00:16:40,170 --> 00:16:41,405
I see.

246
00:16:41,472 --> 00:16:44,575
You helped my mother at first, and then…

247
00:16:45,342 --> 00:16:46,443
That's right.

248
00:16:46,977 --> 00:16:49,480
Who would have thought
a kind-hearted passerby

249
00:16:49,546 --> 00:16:54,485
would turn out to be a detective.

250
00:16:54,551 --> 00:16:59,723
If Sakura is by Mariko's side,
I can rest easy as well.

251
00:16:59,790 --> 00:17:02,926
Please take good care
of her going forward.

252
00:17:02,993 --> 00:17:03,827
Dad!

253
00:17:03,894 --> 00:17:05,729
Please raise your head.

254
00:17:09,366 --> 00:17:11,435
REST IN PEACE

255
00:17:25,749 --> 00:17:27,951
Where were you going, Mariko?

256
00:17:28,852 --> 00:17:30,320
I called, but…

257
00:17:31,221 --> 00:17:33,957
I'm sorry, I was dealing with something.

258
00:17:35,225 --> 00:17:38,996
We should be together as much
as possible until the case is solved.

259
00:17:42,232 --> 00:17:44,001
I know it's annoying.

260
00:17:44,968 --> 00:17:49,506
And I know you clearly told me you didn't
want me walking you home the other day…

261
00:17:51,408 --> 00:17:52,976
But I'm worried.

262
00:17:53,610 --> 00:17:54,912
This time for sure…

263
00:17:57,514 --> 00:17:59,183
I will protect you.

264
00:18:04,054 --> 00:18:05,255
This time?

265
00:18:08,525 --> 00:18:09,560
That reminds me.

266
00:18:10,561 --> 00:18:15,132
Influenced by you,
I've started painting again recently.

267
00:18:15,699 --> 00:18:16,900
Influenced by me?

268
00:18:16,967 --> 00:18:18,235
I'll show you sometime.

269
00:18:21,538 --> 00:18:23,273
SHIRAKI

270
00:18:23,974 --> 00:18:25,108
Excuse me for a moment.

271
00:18:26,643 --> 00:18:28,545
Yes, hello?

272
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:31,215
‎Yes.

273
00:18:32,482 --> 00:18:33,317
‎Yes…

274
00:18:35,786 --> 00:18:36,620
What?

275
00:18:37,821 --> 00:18:38,655
Understood.

276
00:18:40,791 --> 00:18:43,427
Asai has been taken
into protective custody.

277
00:18:44,595 --> 00:18:45,662
What?

278
00:18:53,170 --> 00:18:56,840
If he doesn't regain consciousness soon,
he'll have to be hospitalized even longer.

279
00:18:56,907 --> 00:18:58,442
He will live.

280
00:18:58,976 --> 00:19:00,143
Thank you very much.

281
00:19:00,210 --> 00:19:02,479
-Please take care of him.
-Please.

282
00:19:02,546 --> 00:19:03,580
-Doctor.
-Yes?

283
00:19:03,647 --> 00:19:05,482
-May I have a moment?
-Yes.

284
00:19:10,687 --> 00:19:13,557
To think this could happen to Asai.

285
00:19:14,825 --> 00:19:16,393
Who would do something like this?

286
00:19:19,696 --> 00:19:22,666
Was it the same one
who killed Tateiwa and Sayuri?

287
00:19:24,101 --> 00:19:27,004
That I do not know. However…

288
00:19:31,241 --> 00:19:32,309
No.

289
00:19:32,376 --> 00:19:33,377
What?

290
00:19:34,845 --> 00:19:37,114
You have a lot of secrets.

291
00:19:38,048 --> 00:19:42,185
I came home today because
I wanted to ask you something.

292
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:45,389
Keito said he heard it.

293
00:19:47,324 --> 00:19:50,127
What is the secret you and Sayuri share?

294
00:19:51,695 --> 00:19:53,930
You haven't forgotten, have you?

295
00:19:54,498 --> 00:19:58,368
That you and I share the same secret.

296
00:19:59,870 --> 00:20:02,205
Isn't it something related
to what's happened?

297
00:20:02,739 --> 00:20:04,441
Hey, Dad!

298
00:20:04,508 --> 00:20:06,310
Stop keeping secrets from me!

299
00:20:26,863 --> 00:20:28,198
Which one is it?

300
00:20:31,234 --> 00:20:35,439
Regarding Kagura, we were able to secure
distribution in 100 stores for now.

301
00:20:36,873 --> 00:20:41,311
Also for EC, next Monday
is when they'll buy,

302
00:20:41,378 --> 00:20:45,349
so we at least hope to have
a selection ready for them.

303
00:20:45,415 --> 00:20:47,484
What do we think about that?

304
00:20:50,454 --> 00:20:51,822
Mariko?

305
00:20:55,759 --> 00:20:57,127
Ah, um…

306
00:20:57,194 --> 00:20:58,061
I'm sorry.

307
00:20:58,595 --> 00:20:59,930
One more time, please.

308
00:20:59,996 --> 00:21:00,831
Okay.

309
00:21:01,631 --> 00:21:02,833
Let's see. Previous page…

310
00:21:03,333 --> 00:21:07,571
Regarding Kagura, we were able to secure
distribution in 100 stores for now.

311
00:21:29,192 --> 00:21:30,460
Goodbye, everyone.

312
00:21:30,527 --> 00:21:32,596
-Goodbye.
-See you.

313
00:21:49,679 --> 00:21:50,747
Mariko.

314
00:21:52,282 --> 00:21:54,351
You forgot this on your desk.

315
00:21:54,418 --> 00:21:56,686
Huh? Oh, thank you.

316
00:21:58,121 --> 00:21:59,055
Are you okay?

317
00:21:59,790 --> 00:22:01,158
Did something happen?

318
00:22:03,226 --> 00:22:04,094
I'm sorry.

319
00:22:04,828 --> 00:22:06,196
It's none of my business.

320
00:22:29,653 --> 00:22:30,787
Hello.

321
00:22:32,189 --> 00:22:34,458
-Chairwoman, what brings you here?
-Are you alone?

322
00:22:35,225 --> 00:22:36,526
If you want Mariko, she already…

323
00:22:36,593 --> 00:22:38,495
I came to see you.

324
00:22:43,133 --> 00:22:47,204
The incident with Tateiwa and Sayuri.

325
00:22:48,071 --> 00:22:50,540
I heard you were questioned by the police?

326
00:22:52,342 --> 00:22:53,343
Yes.

327
00:22:54,211 --> 00:22:55,312
Did you do it?

328
00:22:57,481 --> 00:22:59,783
Of course not. I know that.

329
00:23:03,887 --> 00:23:07,457
Is our family cursed or something?

330
00:23:08,058 --> 00:23:09,693
Two daughters-in-law.

331
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:14,464
Even a daughter-in-law I hated
so much, for her to die like that…

332
00:23:15,332 --> 00:23:17,567
Why did you hate her so much?

333
00:23:19,703 --> 00:23:21,304
Sorry, I shouldn't pry.

334
00:23:23,406 --> 00:23:26,776
Kyoko, Mariko's biological mother,

335
00:23:27,410 --> 00:23:29,045
was suspected of having an affair.

336
00:23:29,679 --> 00:23:30,514
What?

337
00:23:30,580 --> 00:23:35,318
I don't know who it was with,
but Ginjiro seemed to suspect

338
00:23:35,385 --> 00:23:37,787
it was with a younger man.

339
00:23:38,455 --> 00:23:40,824
I think that was a lie.

340
00:23:41,691 --> 00:23:42,959
And yet,

341
00:23:43,627 --> 00:23:47,731
Sayuri said that to young Mariko,

342
00:23:48,298 --> 00:23:52,836
of all places, at Kyoko's funeral.

343
00:23:53,537 --> 00:23:58,174
Your mother fell in love with another man.

344
00:23:59,442 --> 00:24:00,610
Poor thing.

345
00:24:03,613 --> 00:24:05,348
Thinking about what feelings

346
00:24:06,716 --> 00:24:09,719
Mariko has lived with since then.

347
00:24:09,786 --> 00:24:11,955
Mariko's mother wasn't
that kind of person.

348
00:24:12,522 --> 00:24:13,790
It's definitely not true.

349
00:24:15,492 --> 00:24:16,826
I know Mariko's mother.

350
00:24:18,962 --> 00:24:19,863
Um…

351
00:24:20,564 --> 00:24:22,365
I've been…

352
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:25,669
I've been watching Mariko this whole time.

353
00:24:26,369 --> 00:24:27,304
What?

354
00:24:28,371 --> 00:24:29,973
I wanted to be with Mariko,

355
00:24:30,040 --> 00:24:32,375
so I went to the same middle school,
high school, university,

356
00:24:33,243 --> 00:24:36,746
and even followed her to the same company.

357
00:24:38,114 --> 00:24:40,550
But I could never talk to her even once.

358
00:24:42,118 --> 00:24:43,720
All I could do was just watch her.

359
00:24:46,790 --> 00:24:48,024
I've loved…

360
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:52,128
Mariko for so long.

361
00:24:54,464 --> 00:24:57,500
Confessing to me isn't going to do much.

362
00:24:59,269 --> 00:25:02,739
Do you love Mariko that much?

363
00:25:04,307 --> 00:25:06,042
Yes, I'm sorry.

364
00:25:07,143 --> 00:25:10,380
Hearing someone say
they love my grandchild

365
00:25:10,447 --> 00:25:12,582
doesn't feel bad.

366
00:25:13,984 --> 00:25:15,585
She's a good girl, isn't she?

367
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:20,824
But if you love her so much,
why didn't you ever speak to her?

368
00:25:22,425 --> 00:25:26,596
There must have been plenty of times
you could have said something.

369
00:25:26,663 --> 00:25:27,831
Well, that's…

370
00:25:28,965 --> 00:25:32,235
Mariko is someone I admire, so…

371
00:25:33,503 --> 00:25:35,071
Just watching her was enough.

372
00:25:35,605 --> 00:25:38,908
If Mariko was happy,
that alone made me happy.

373
00:25:40,877 --> 00:25:42,612
You're not being honest.

374
00:25:45,315 --> 00:25:51,521
When things don't go well,
the cause is always within yourself.

375
00:25:52,589 --> 00:25:57,060
You shouldn't look for answers
inside the other person.

376
00:26:12,175 --> 00:26:13,610
Sorry about that.

377
00:26:15,879 --> 00:26:17,247
Wait here a second.

378
00:26:18,548 --> 00:26:19,783
Ah, no, no, it's fine.

379
00:26:19,849 --> 00:26:21,284
It'd be terrible if you got hurt.

380
00:26:27,724 --> 00:26:30,593
It's rare to see you irritated.

381
00:26:32,662 --> 00:26:33,763
Sorry.

382
00:26:34,931 --> 00:26:36,399
Days like that happen.

383
00:26:36,466 --> 00:26:37,701
We're human, after all.

384
00:26:44,874 --> 00:26:45,709
After all?

385
00:26:47,343 --> 00:26:50,046
I get irritated all the time.

386
00:26:50,113 --> 00:26:51,614
Like when everything doesn't fit

387
00:26:51,681 --> 00:26:54,184
into the reusable bag
I brought to the supermarket

388
00:26:54,250 --> 00:26:56,686
and I have to buy a plastic bag.

389
00:26:57,754 --> 00:27:01,858
Or thinking, "Ah, I didn't even need
to buy this mirin today, damn it."

390
00:27:02,892 --> 00:27:07,130
Or when an elevator door is closing,

391
00:27:07,197 --> 00:27:12,635
and someone rushes up, hits the button
to force it open, and gets in.

392
00:27:14,571 --> 00:27:16,606
I guess that's not being irritated.

393
00:27:16,673 --> 00:27:18,942
That's just me having a bad personality.

394
00:27:22,545 --> 00:27:23,713
Thank you.

395
00:27:26,616 --> 00:27:28,718
If you want to talk about it, I'll listen.

396
00:27:33,923 --> 00:27:34,924
Mama!

397
00:27:38,261 --> 00:27:39,129
Coming.

398
00:27:40,630 --> 00:27:42,132
What were you talking about?

399
00:27:42,198 --> 00:27:45,068
Huh? It's a secret. Let's go home.

400
00:28:05,355 --> 00:28:07,056
SATORU HATANO

401
00:28:07,123 --> 00:28:08,725
HE MAY BE DANGEROUS

402
00:28:08,792 --> 00:28:12,862
HE'S THE ONE WHO TRIED TO KIDNAP MARIKO

403
00:29:43,620 --> 00:29:45,054
MARIKO NOSE

404
00:29:53,096 --> 00:29:55,965
COME QUICK
I'LL KILL HER IF YOU TELL ANYONE

405
00:30:23,426 --> 00:30:24,560
Mariko!

406
00:31:16,512 --> 00:31:18,281
GOTO ASAI - NOSE COSMETICS

407
00:31:24,087 --> 00:31:25,755
MARIKO NOSE - NOSE COSMETICS

408
00:31:35,732 --> 00:31:38,001
-The number you have dialed…
-Shit…

409
00:31:55,985 --> 00:31:57,720
It's okay.

410
00:31:59,455 --> 00:32:02,291
I won't kill you, princess.

411
00:32:03,292 --> 00:32:06,963
Well, if I end up killing you
along the way, my bad.

412
00:32:12,001 --> 00:32:14,370
You've gotten big.

413
00:32:16,205 --> 00:32:17,607
What on earth

414
00:32:18,674 --> 00:32:20,143
are you planning to do?

415
00:32:25,081 --> 00:32:26,482
Mariko!

416
00:32:26,549 --> 00:32:29,152
Yukimura! Why?

417
00:32:29,218 --> 00:32:31,154
You finally showed up.

418
00:32:31,220 --> 00:32:33,056
Get away from Mariko.

419
00:32:34,257 --> 00:32:36,826
-Get away!
-It's fine.

420
00:32:36,893 --> 00:32:38,761
Calm down.

421
00:32:38,828 --> 00:32:41,264
The one getting killed is you, after all.

422
00:32:43,900 --> 00:32:46,436
I've wanted to meet you
for a long time, boy.

423
00:32:47,937 --> 00:32:51,841
Thanks to that courageous action of yours,

424
00:32:51,908 --> 00:32:54,677
I had to spend 25 years in prison.

425
00:32:55,945 --> 00:32:58,081
Coming out after all this time,

426
00:32:58,147 --> 00:33:02,718
the world has changed
so much that it blew my mind.

427
00:33:02,785 --> 00:33:05,288
Even in Shibuya,
there aren't any kogals left at all.

428
00:33:05,354 --> 00:33:07,857
And it's Toyosu Market now, not Tsukiji.

429
00:33:08,691 --> 00:33:11,761
The biggest thing is security cameras.

430
00:33:12,295 --> 00:33:13,996
They're everywhere.

431
00:33:14,897 --> 00:33:18,167
You can't just easily kidnap
someone like in the old days.

432
00:33:18,835 --> 00:33:21,571
It's a tough world to live in. Right?

433
00:33:23,106 --> 00:33:27,009
But some things don't change.

434
00:33:28,945 --> 00:33:31,247
I was moved, boy.

435
00:33:32,381 --> 00:33:34,784
I thought you were just
some kid passing by,

436
00:33:34,851 --> 00:33:38,788
but here you are even now,
coming to save the princess in a pinch.

437
00:33:40,022 --> 00:33:42,391
You're a fine hero.

438
00:33:44,894 --> 00:33:47,697
Makes it worth doing for me too.

439
00:33:48,531 --> 00:33:51,234
I understand very well
that your target is me.

440
00:33:51,767 --> 00:33:54,470
So please let Mariko go right now.

441
00:33:54,537 --> 00:33:56,706
After that, you can kill me.

442
00:33:56,772 --> 00:33:58,307
What are you saying?

443
00:33:59,742 --> 00:34:01,110
You're amazing.

444
00:34:02,278 --> 00:34:04,847
You're a far braver boy than I imagined.

445
00:34:04,914 --> 00:34:07,717
Stop it! Yukimura, run away, quick!

446
00:34:07,783 --> 00:34:09,986
Please let Mariko go.

447
00:34:10,720 --> 00:34:12,822
How cool.

448
00:34:13,322 --> 00:34:18,194
But wouldn't showing her
a man dying for her sake

449
00:34:18,261 --> 00:34:19,962
be even cooler?

450
00:34:20,029 --> 00:34:22,665
Right?

451
00:34:22,732 --> 00:34:23,599
Don't move.

452
00:34:48,157 --> 00:34:49,091
Mariko.

453
00:34:49,158 --> 00:34:50,593
Are you okay?

454
00:34:56,599 --> 00:34:57,667
Yukimura, behind you!

455
00:35:05,074 --> 00:35:09,011
You've got a disastrous life too.

456
00:35:10,146 --> 00:35:11,214
If you hadn't

457
00:35:12,014 --> 00:35:14,617
witnessed this princess'
kidnapping back then,

458
00:35:14,684 --> 00:35:17,220
you wouldn't have to die here.

459
00:35:18,387 --> 00:35:20,590
My life…

460
00:35:21,190 --> 00:35:23,226
isn't a disaster!

461
00:35:29,632 --> 00:35:30,366
Yukimura!

462
00:35:37,873 --> 00:35:39,342
Yukimura!

463
00:36:34,096 --> 00:36:36,165
That hurt!

464
00:36:36,799 --> 00:36:37,633
Mariko…

465
00:36:43,105 --> 00:36:44,140
Mariko!

466
00:36:45,508 --> 00:36:48,744
Hey, stay back.

467
00:36:48,811 --> 00:36:50,212
Get away from Mariko!

468
00:36:52,748 --> 00:36:54,216
Police!

469
00:36:55,384 --> 00:36:58,054
Hatano, release the hostage.

470
00:37:00,523 --> 00:37:01,624
Release her, now!

471
00:37:03,426 --> 00:37:05,494
-Shut up!
-Don't move!

472
00:37:06,829 --> 00:37:07,963
Get back.

473
00:37:08,998 --> 00:37:10,366
Go away!

474
00:37:10,433 --> 00:37:12,501
Go away!

475
00:37:12,568 --> 00:37:14,303
-Let her go!
-Stay back!

476
00:37:17,406 --> 00:37:19,008
Stop! Hatano, stop!

477
00:37:19,075 --> 00:37:20,976
Mariko, are you okay?

478
00:37:21,477 --> 00:37:23,212
-Are you hurt?
-I'm fine.

479
00:37:23,279 --> 00:37:24,914
You're not okay, though, evidently.

480
00:37:26,148 --> 00:37:29,485
One man fled the scene, two victims.

481
00:37:29,552 --> 00:37:30,720
They're conscious.

482
00:37:30,786 --> 00:37:32,655
Requesting an ambulance.

483
00:37:35,124 --> 00:37:36,926
Mariko, are you hurt?

484
00:37:36,992 --> 00:37:38,928
I'm fine.

485
00:37:38,994 --> 00:37:40,162
Thank goodness…

486
00:37:41,964 --> 00:37:42,865
Sorry…

487
00:37:42,932 --> 00:37:44,066
Yukimura…

488
00:37:52,308 --> 00:37:53,576
I'll tie it.

489
00:37:57,213 --> 00:37:59,181
An ambulance will be here shortly.

490
00:37:59,248 --> 00:38:00,282
Okay.

491
00:38:10,059 --> 00:38:13,562
‎POLICE

492
00:38:13,629 --> 00:38:16,899
‎STOPPING CRIME

493
00:38:38,287 --> 00:38:40,055
Why would you do something that dangerous?

494
00:38:42,291 --> 00:38:46,295
You could've contacted the police
or anything else, right?

495
00:38:47,530 --> 00:38:48,564
I'm sorry.

496
00:38:57,440 --> 00:38:58,374
You…

497
00:39:01,210 --> 00:39:04,613
were the boy
who saved me back then, right?

498
00:39:09,185 --> 00:39:10,019
Yes.

499
00:39:12,388 --> 00:39:13,289
Why?

500
00:39:17,893 --> 00:39:19,094
Why didn't you say anything?

501
00:39:24,400 --> 00:39:26,235
You could have told me at any point.

502
00:39:27,236 --> 00:39:31,407
Twenty-five years ago, or even since
we've known each other.

503
00:39:42,117 --> 00:39:44,487
I had no courage.

504
00:39:45,988 --> 00:39:50,526
Ever since I was a child, I was the kind
of kid who couldn't even talk back

505
00:39:50,593 --> 00:39:52,027
when classmates made fun of me.

506
00:39:54,029 --> 00:39:57,132
Even if I talked to you,
I didn't think you'd like me.

507
00:39:58,000 --> 00:39:59,134
In fact…

508
00:40:01,237 --> 00:40:02,872
I thought you might hate me.

509
00:40:05,841 --> 00:40:07,343
But I…

510
00:40:10,312 --> 00:40:12,348
I'd always wanted to talk to you,

511
00:40:14,216 --> 00:40:15,684
but I didn't have the courage.

512
00:40:18,954 --> 00:40:20,656
Even though you can do
something like this?

513
00:40:23,926 --> 00:40:26,695
I can't do anything for myself.

514
00:40:29,198 --> 00:40:31,000
But if it's for your sake, Mariko…

515
00:40:34,470 --> 00:40:36,972
That's what scares you, isn't it?

516
00:40:37,039 --> 00:40:38,140
I'm sorry.

517
00:40:39,008 --> 00:40:39,875
No,

518
00:40:40,676 --> 00:40:42,177
it's not that you scare me.

519
00:40:45,214 --> 00:40:48,851
It's that I don't know
who the real you is anymore.

520
00:40:50,152 --> 00:40:51,520
That's why I got scared.

521
00:40:53,322 --> 00:40:56,625
I mean, like with Marvel
and cafes and stuff,

522
00:40:57,192 --> 00:40:59,728
you only liked them
because I liked them, right?

523
00:41:00,329 --> 00:41:02,364
That's not the real you.

524
00:41:25,154 --> 00:41:26,055
This…

525
00:41:27,990 --> 00:41:29,058
is me.

526
00:41:32,328 --> 00:41:36,165
I came to like what you liked,

527
00:41:38,467 --> 00:41:40,135
look at the scenery you looked at.

528
00:41:41,670 --> 00:41:43,339
That's how I've lived.

529
00:41:48,077 --> 00:41:51,981
If I lose you, Mariko,
I will have nothing left in my life.

530
00:41:53,882 --> 00:41:56,919
Because ever since you appeared
in my life, right up to today…

531
00:42:01,323 --> 00:42:03,993
I've always been happy.

532
00:42:08,430 --> 00:42:11,667
I'm living my own life…

533
00:42:16,505 --> 00:42:18,374
but you've always been in it, Mariko.

534
00:42:23,912 --> 00:42:25,014
I'm sorry.

535
00:42:27,149 --> 00:42:29,051
For watching over you for 25 years…

536
00:42:31,420 --> 00:42:33,288
without you asking me to.

537
00:42:38,694 --> 00:42:40,095
I'm sorry.

538
00:42:47,803 --> 00:42:49,538
You really are scary.

539
00:43:24,606 --> 00:43:28,677
-Ready? Let's go.
-Yes.

540
00:43:29,478 --> 00:43:32,981
Whoa, Mom's going to get mad at us.

541
00:43:33,048 --> 00:43:34,516
Because you're terrible at this.

542
00:43:35,350 --> 00:43:37,352
That's because you didn't
catch it properly, Tomoya!

543
00:43:37,419 --> 00:43:40,089
-You suck!
-Shut up!

544
00:44:16,792 --> 00:44:18,360
Wait, wait!

545
00:44:19,728 --> 00:44:22,931
Wait, wait!

546
00:44:22,998 --> 00:44:24,867
Wait, you're too fast!

547
00:44:33,742 --> 00:44:36,945
There has been a sudden development
in the kidnappings in Setagaya.

548
00:44:37,012 --> 00:44:40,616
Four children were taken in total.

549
00:44:40,682 --> 00:44:43,819
It has been confirmed that one
third-grade girl who went missing has died

550
00:44:43,886 --> 00:44:44,987
in a warehouse.

551
00:44:45,053 --> 00:44:47,055
The arrested suspect is the unemployed

552
00:44:47,122 --> 00:44:49,591
Satoru Hatano.

553
00:44:49,658 --> 00:44:51,994
MIZUKI SAGARA

554
00:44:58,567 --> 00:45:03,505
‎NEXT TIME…

